c/texas/falls-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids July to August came in under 90% of normal in 38 of 75 years. In 2025 the county&rsquo;s middle value had June to July at 177% of normal and November to December at 46%. For 2026, February to March is published at 33% of normal on the county&rsquo;s middle value. Grid 13331 had its driest year in 1954 at 44%.</p>"}
